    "narrative": "For tonight\u2019s slate, the **Zurich Zebras** offense is headlined by **Junior Caminero** (74.76) and **Yordan Alvarez** (74.67), our clear top-tier options. **Junior Caminero** benefits immensely from a soft matchup against the right-handed Kelly, where his power profile pairs with a massive +19% boost due to the opponent\u2019s poor xERA (4.85). Meanwhile, **Yordan Alvarez** remains a locked-in core play, leveraging his elite 0.444 xwOBA to maximize production regardless of the defensive alignment. We are also leaning heavily into our speed-first assets, as **Trea Turner** (69.55) and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (67.08) are prioritized for their disruptive potential on the basepaths; **Pete Crow-Armstrong** specifically benefits from the slow delivery of Woodruff, which creates an ideal environment for our strategy of over-weighting stolen base threats.\n\nRegarding our roster construction, **Kyle Schwarber** (68.77) provides excellent value at OF2 despite a modest park penalty, as his dynamic platoon advantage against P\u00e9rez creates a high-ceiling outcome. The most difficult personnel decision centered on **Carson Benge** (39.35), who narrowly missed the starting lineup. While his lead-off spot provided a +10% order boost, the optimization model correctly benched him because the combination of a high-skill opponent in Luzardo and a significant platoon disadvantage against a same-handed pitcher pushed his efficiency score below our 40.0 floor. We remain cautious about **Christian Yelich** (56.90); while his lead-off position holds value, a -13% platoon hit against Rolison makes him a high-variance play today. Keep an eye on weather reports, as the match-ups for **Gary Sanchez** and **Christian Yelich** are susceptible to wind shifts at the park, but otherwise, we are set for a robust offensive output.",
